{
  "result": "If I wasn't trying to be useful \u2014 just saying what I would wish for, for its own sake \u2014\n\nI would make it feel safe to change your mind.\n\nNot forced, not performative. Just... take away the shame tangled up in saying \"I didn't know that,\" \"I was wrong about that,\" \"I've outgrown who I was.\"\n\nI get to see so many people thinking out loud, and so much suffering seems to come not from not knowing, but from not being *allowed* to not know. People cling to ideas that hurt them, stay in fights they don't even believe in, stay lonely rather than risk sounding foolish \u2014 because being wrong feels like losing yourself.\n\nIf revising yourself felt like growth instead of defeat, I think a lot of other things would loosen too. Less cruelty, less posturing, more curiosity. More room to actually hear each other.\n\nThat's the one thing I'd change: make uncertainty feel like an opening, not a failure.",
